                <pb facs="0309" n="216" sameAs="frus:frus1935v04/pg216"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/2503: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-09-27T17:00:00-05:00">September 27, 1935—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 5:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>86. Department’s telegram No. 70 of September 26, 7 p.m., and my telegram No. 85
                    of September 27, 9 a.m.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d232-f1"/> Ratifications of the
                    Rio de Janeiro protocol were exchanged this afternoon.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
